Dear Wim,

Assuming that I'm interpreting correctly what you mean by subsetting a 
list, the solution is to use single-bracket indexing. After all, if you 
select more than one element of a list, then the result should be a list. 
For example

        > x[c(1,2)]
        $a:
        [1] 1 2 3

        $b:
        [1] 100

I hope that this is what you need,
 John

