> step-by-step command lines info for the estimation. Please
> help!
>
>

If the errors are independent and normally distributed with constant
variance, then the ML estimator is just the usual least-squares
estimator, most easily obtained in S as lm(y ~ x1 + x2). If the situation
is more complicated, then you have to supply some more
information.

I hope that this helps,

