To merge two data frames, both need to have at least one
extra column in addition of the ones used in the by argument:

spcode.sfr$dummy<-rep(0,nrow(spcode.sfr))
merge(spcode.sfr, smk99[,22:25], by="SPCODE")

If you are trying to select rows in the main data set containing
info about a list of species, you can simply do

smk99[is.element(smk99$SPCODE,spcode.sfr$SPCODE),22:25]

Gabriel

Are you sure that the codes are the same in both datasets? In
particular, is there a space character before species
like " TEIJCO" in your main dataset? It seems that
only species without that character are merged?

